# Rolls-Royce Phantom II, 1929-1935.
#
# The Phantom II: 7,668 cc pushrod six, wheelbase 3,683 mm (3,810 mm on the
# long chassis), overall dimensions body-dependent (about 5,300 x 1,800 x
# 1,750 mm as a saloon). About 1,680 built, the pinnacle of the pre-war
# Rolls-Royce and a class-4 model of the 1930s.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rolls-Royce_Phantom_II
#
# Colours: Black, Dark Green, Maroon and Grey are documented period finishes.
#
# Weight: 12 in total (black 5, green 3, maroon 2, grey 2). Section F: early
# prestige models are representative only.
#
# Speed 130 km/h; comfort 75/443 (line). Class 4.
# Dates: 1929-1935 with a road tail to about 1955.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rolls-royce-phantom-ii.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rolls-royce-phantom-ii/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia
# Commons.

obj=citycar
name=RollsRoycePhantomII(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=5
intro_year=1929
intro_month=9
retire_year=1955
retire_month=6
speed=130
class=4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=75
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=443

